  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Anti-Corruption Basket Fund</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Anti-Corruption Basket Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">The Pan-American Development Foundation (PADF/FUPAD) i Colombia har ans&#xf6;kt om finansiering fr&#xe5;n Sida om 4 800 000 SEK f&#xf6;r perioden 2017&#x2013;2020. Insatsen &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att st&#xf6;dja offentlig antikorruptionspolitik, medborgerlig delaktighet och ansvarsutkr&#xe4;vande f&#xf6;r att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra offentlig f&#xf6;rvaltning, samh&#xe4;llsservice och transparens. Insatsen har tre specifika m&#xe5;l: 1) Fr&#xe4;mja medborgarnas deltagande genom att st&#xe4;rka m&#xe4;nniskors kunskap och f&#xf6;rm&#xe5;ga att bek&#xe4;mpa korruption. 2) St&#xe4;rka offentliga institutioner s&#xe5; att de inf&#xf6;rlivar f&#xf6;rfaranden som fr&#xe4;mjar administrativ effektivitet, b&#xe4;sta praxis och transparens, och 3) Fr&#xe4;mja f&#xf6;rtroendeskapande och transparanta processer genom att underl&#xe4;tta dialogen mellan medborgare och offentligt anst&#xe4;llda.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Pan-American Development Foundation (PADF/FUPAD) in Colombia has applied to Sida for funding of 4 800 000 SEK during the period 2017-2020.  The overall objective of the intervention is to promote anti-corruption policies, citizen participation and accountability to improve public management, service delivery and transparency. The intervention has three specific objectives: 1. Promoting citizen participation by strengthening people&#x2019;s knowledge and capabilities to fight against corruption; 2. Strengthening public institutions to incorporate procedures that promote administrative efficiency, best practices and transparency; and 3. Fostering trust-building and transparency processes, by facilitating dialogue between citizens and public servants.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the intervention is to promote anti-corruption policies, citizen participation and accountability to improve public management, service delivery and transparecy.&#xa0;
The intervention has three specific objectives:&#xa0;
1. Promoting citizen participation by strengthening people&#x2019;s knowledge and capabilities to fight against corruption.
2. Strengthening public institutions to incorporate procedures that promote administrative efficiency, best practices and transparency.
3. Fostering trust-building and transparency processes, by facilitating dialogue between citizens and public servants.</narrative>
  </description>
